            <ArticleTitle>[Acute abdomen caused by jejunal perforation as a clinical presentation of MEN-1 syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of acute abdomen due to a jejunal perforation. The final diagnosis was concluded a multiple endocrine neoplasia type I. In the literature reviewed, no similar clinical presentation was found. We review the diagnostic sequence and the management of these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
